<string name="Text">LocalScripts run on your device and their actions are usually not seen by the server or by other players unless it remote calls a Server Event.  Studio Lite automatically inserts a prewritten LocalScript when you insert a server Script that needs a remote call.  The GuiHideLocal is a handy way to close a Gui when the player is done reading it, if no server interaction is needed.  If the server does need to act on the click, insert the Script (not localscript): GuiActivatedScript.  It will automatically insert a child LocalScript to activate the button.</string>
